{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>A lion's whelp is Judah.</b> Behold Judah — even though he is not a lion, for he has no kingship, he is indeed a lion's whelp: he prevails over his brothers and is destined to reign. And despite this:" "<b>From the prey, my son, you have gone up.</b> You, Joseph my son, went up from his prey — he did not tear you in his anger to kill you, even though he hated you. And this is because <b>he stooped, he crouched like a lion</b> — he was then like a lion that stoops and crouches without causing harm; so too he then did not order you put to death." "<b>And as a lioness, who shall rouse him?</b> So it shall be in his future kingship: he shall crouch like a lioness, and there shall be none able to cast terror upon him so as to rouse him from his place out of fear."], :book :genesis, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:35:16.155581414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}